[h1]Relic Reshuffle[/h1]

Every time you enter a fight, your relics are reshuffled into [b]different relics of the same rarity[/b]. A common becomes another common, a rare another rare — your relic count and overall power never change, only [i]which[/i] relics you are holding. They stay until the next fight.

A [b]⇄ button in the top bar[/b] appears during combat and shows what became what.

[h2]What stays put[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Starter relics[/b] and [b]Circlet[/b]
[*][b]Ancient[/b] and [b]event[/b] relics — each can be opted in (off by default)
[*][b]Wax relics[/b] — they are about to melt, so they are not traded for permanent ones
[*][b]Relics you paid to re-forge or cleanse[/b]
[*][b]Relics added by other mods[/b] — what that mod gave you is still there next fight
[*][b]Relics outside your character's relic pool[/b] — nothing is taken that cannot be given back
[/list]

Everything else of that rarity is in the pool. There is no curation by usefulness.

[h2]Relics with a pickup effect[/h2]
Strawberry, Mango and the like can come up. One handed to you by a reshuffle does not fire its effect — doing so would mint permanent stats every fight — and its tooltip says so. If you already collected that effect this run, obtaining the relic again does nothing, and that covers gold, card upgrades and enchantments too.

[h2]Your pool never shrinks[/h2]
A relic the reshuffle takes away goes back into the pool and can appear in shops and rewards again. Owning something once never narrows your options.

[h2]With other mods[/h2]
Restart and undo mods are handled — re-entering a fight re-applies the same reshuffle rather than skipping it.

[h2]Co-op[/h2]
Supported. Both players reshuffle together, and the host's settings apply.

